---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL } from "../lib/site";
---

<Layout
  title="Build Not Codex from source"
  description="Build the early Not Codex work in progress from its public source repository."
>
  <div class="build-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Not Codex / Early access</p>
    <h1>Build from source</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Packaged downloads and a hosted app are not public yet. Today, the honest way to try Not Codex
      is to review and build the source yourself with any supported provider harness.
    </p>

    <div class="build-grid">
      <section>
        <span>01</span>
        <h2>Requirements</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Node.js 24.13 or newer on the Node 24 release line</li>
          <li><a href="https://viteplus.dev/guide/">Vite+</a></li>
          <li>Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, Grok Build, OpenCode, or Pi</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section>
        <span>02</span>
        <h2>Run locally</h2>
        <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/MaTriXy/not-codex.git
cd not-codex
vp install
vp run dev</code></pre>
      </section>
    </div>

    <aside class="warning" role="note">
      Not Codex is an early work in progress. Use repositories you can recover, inspect agent actions,
      and do not expose the local server to an untrusted network.
    </aside>

    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href={GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}>Browse source on GitHub</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={`${GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}/blob/main/docs/getting-started/quick-start.md`}>Read the quick start</a>
    </div>
    <p class="availability">Signed desktop packages and hosted access are planned, not promised.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .build-page { width: min(920px, calc(100% - 40px)); margin: 0 auto; padding: clamp(72px, 10vw, 128px) 0 112px; }
  h1 { margin-top: 16px; font-size: clamp(3.6rem, 9vw, 7rem); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.05em; line-height: 0.92; }
  .lede { max-width: 700px; margin-top: 30px; color: var(--fg-muted); font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.3rem); line-height: 1.65; }
  .build-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr; gap: 20px; margin-top: 64px; }
  section { min-width: 0; padding: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--bg-card); }
  section > span { color: var(--accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; }
  h2 { margin-top: 12px; font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 500; }
  ul { margin: 22px 0 0 20px; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.9; }
  li a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  pre { margin-top: 22px; overflow-x: auto; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); background: #08080a; padding: 18px; color: var(--ink-on-dark); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.82rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .warning { margin-top: 20px; padding: 18px 20px; border-left: 3px solid var(--warn); background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.025); color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.65; }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 32px; }
  .availability { margin-top: 18px; color: var(--fg-dim); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .build-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } section { padding: 22px; } }
</style>
